      {
        "attempt": 1,
        "status": "OK",
        "asr_text": "Imagine trying to focus when a familiar phone alert sounds. You do not look at the screen, you do not touch the phone, but your attention may still move toward it. A 2022 study tested this idea with 73 university students. They completed 960 rounds of a visual letter task. Some rounds included a notification sound, others included a neutral comparison sound. The result was clear: people responded more slowly when the notification sound played. Brainwave recordings also showed a stronger signal during those rounds. The researchers interpreted this as a sign that extra mental control was needed to keep working.",
        "instruction_type": "english_style_prefix_wide_margin",
        "audio_classification": "NORMALIZED_MATCH",
        "length_ok": true,
        "verified": true,
        "trim_info": {
